Subject: Cantor Self Work Update Broker B1 Npm Native Preparation P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] d3ab9189-a42c-48fe-8850-6dcf916a6259
@ [canonical_uuid] e195bf96-a4ea-4142-b58f-3d189b726ed9

& [Why]
  + B1 cannot truthfully lock generated-schema environment root or canary facts until one selected host has a separately authorized disposable fixture
  + the user has now closed executable recovery-owner and preparation-root choice by authorizing the recommended npm-native commission
  + a preparation-only SJS keeps the mutating fixture and schema producer distinct from the later read-only B1 observer

& [SmallestSurface]
  + one absent fixed envelope one deterministic local candidate one nonsecret canary set one direct schema command one retained result
  + no generic launcher wrapper selection provider route model call network proof cleanup or final-preflight semantics

& [ProductJoin]
  + the result closes concrete inputs needed for Cantor's physical update broker while preserving the host and recovery boundaries required before Cantor can supervise its own work safely
